# App links (docs/app-links-plan.md L5): a URL the platform hands this
# app, warm and cold, on the task manager. The scheme is the DEFAULT one
# — guests/assets/identity.toml declares no `[links]` table, so the app
# owns `<declared id>://…` and every lane drives that (§4).
#
# `open_link` asks the PLATFORM to open the URL from inside this process,
# so the delivery comes back through the door a user's tap takes, with no
# runner involvement. `relaunch link` is the COLD door: act one ends, and
# the runner starts the app THROUGH the platform with the URL, so the two
# lines after it run in a process that was started by the link.
expect_title "tasks"

# A task link opens that task's details. The reference href is the
# per-task observable tasks.steps already reads.
open_link "dev.kaya.aurora.notes://task/t2"
expect_entries 1
expect_href label@reference "https://example.com/tasks/t2"
back
expect_entries 0

# A section link selects the section by name.
open_link "dev.kaya.aurora.notes://today"
expect_section "Today"

# A key no task carries opens Inbox and SAYS the link named nothing —
# the standing rule that nothing is dropped in silence (L4).
open_link "dev.kaya.aurora.notes://task/nope"
expect_section "Inbox"
expect label@link_note "no task named nope"
open_link "dev.kaya.aurora.notes://nothing/here"
expect_section "Inbox"
expect label@link_note "no route for dev.kaya.aurora.notes://nothing/here"

# THE COLD DOOR. Everything after this line is act two, in the process
# the platform starts on the link.
relaunch link "dev.kaya.aurora.notes://task/t1"
# A BEAT BEFORE THE ASSERTIONS, because act two is what a COLD tap looks
# like and the platform needs one: the window composites ~520ms after the
# launch while these two steps finish in ~200ms, so without this the
# process publishes and leaves before anything is drawn — green, with
# nothing on screen (docs/app-links-plan.md L5, measured 2026-09-09).
settle 800
expect_entries 1
expect_href label@reference "https://example.com/tasks/t1"
